Patch 2059: render_frame binds the 16-bit colour texture formats that patch 2020 records (A1R5G5B5, A4R4G4B4, R5G6B5,
R5G5B5A1, D1R5G5B5, D8R8G8B8) (TEX16_BIND=0 off).

The record path took them, but render_frame's format list did not, so such a unit stayed a NULL SRV and sampled zero.
J-Stars' character shaders read small A4R4G4B4 lighting ramps (128x32, 32x32) and got black, so skin and hair came out
far too dark once patch 2056 let those shaders compile. The fight HUD's team flames (same formats) appear again too.

Tested (US disc, quick route, intro cards every 4 s, TEX_BINDDBG=300): NULL SRV units 0 (before: 300 in the first
intro cards, all fmt 0x83/0xA3); faces lit and coloured (bench/exp/2026-11-08_1857-tex16bind, bench/faces_2059.png).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
index 61851cc6..1a383cc6 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
@@ -6155,10 +6155,15 @@ static void render_frame(void)
                 u32 _bf = dr->tex[_u].fmt & 0x9F;
                 /* The formats d3d12_bind_texture records. A half-float one
                  * that is not a render target found above is guest data too. */
+                /* 2059 (TEX16_BIND=0 off): also the 16-bit colour formats patch 2020 records. Without them such a unit
+                 * stayed a NULL SRV and sampled zero: J-Stars' character shaders read their A4R4G4B4 lighting ramps
+                 * (128x32, 32x32 on units 1-3) as black, so skin and hair came out far too dark. */
+                static int t16b = -1; if (t16b < 0) { const char* e = getenv("TEX16_BIND"); t16b = (e && *e == '0') ? 0 : 1; }
+                const int t16 = t16b && (_bf == 0x82 || _bf == 0x83 || _bf == 0x84 || _bf == 0x97 || _bf == 0x9D || _bf == 0x9E);
                 if (dr->tex[_u].off &&
                     (_bf == 0x81 || _bf == 0x85 || _bf == 0x8B ||
                      (_bf >= 0x86 && _bf <= 0x88) || _bf == 0x9A ||
-                     _bf == 0x94 || _bf == 0x95 || _bf == 0x9C || _bf == 0x9F)) {
+                     _bf == 0x94 || _bf == 0x95 || _bf == 0x9C || _bf == 0x9F || t16)) {
                     double _tt = perf_on() ? perf_now() : 0.0;
                     int _cube = dr->tex[_u].cube && (dr_cube_mask(dr) & (1u << _u));
                     int ts = vp_upload_tex_slot(dr->tex[_u].off, dr->tex[_u].w,
